{"id":"chatcmpl-485becc6-7612-45f5-89a8-b8bfa15fe26b","object":"chat.completion","created":1795251776,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task resolves a binary laterality question (right vs. left diaphragm elevation) on a chest X-ray by consulting multiple independent visual-question-answering models and requiring agreement before committing. The strategy emphasizes cross-model corroboration and explicit laterality verification rather than relying on a single inference. Success came from querying specialized and general medical VQA tools in parallel and confirming consensus.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task asks to choose between two laterality-specific findings, explicitly query for the side (right vs. left) rather than the general finding, so the model must commit to a side.\",\n    \"Use two or more independent visual-question-answering models on the same image and accept an answer only when they agree, to reduce single-model error.\",\n    \"Route the question to a domain-specialized expert tool first, then cross-check with a general medical VQA model for corroboration.\",\n    \"For binary medical image questions, phrase the tool query to restate the exact decision axis (e.g., 'which hemidiaphragm is elevated') so the returned answer maps directly to an option.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical image binary classification\": \"Ask each model to state the specific side/finding explicitly, then require agreement across at least two independent models before answering.\",\n    \"Laterality-sensitive questions\": \"Always include the words 'right' and 'left' in the query and confirm the model's answer names a side, not just 'elevated diaphragm'.\",\n    \"Multi-tool consensus\": \"Prefer specialized expert tools for the primary read and general models as a second opinion; treat disagreement as a signal to re-query rather than guess.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm at least two independent tools/models returned the same laterality before finalizing the answer.\",\n    \"Verify the chosen option letter matches the side named by the models (right = A, left = B in this task).\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":432,"total_tokens":847,"completion_tokens":415,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":432},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":415}}}